": "Consolidation of independent and Democratic voters behind Peterson, or any late scandal touching Fulcher, could narrow the margin, though a flip remains unlikely.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Newest usable poll is 83 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Russ Fulcher (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Idaho's 1st District is one of the most Republican-leaning seats in the country, and incumbent Russ Fulcher is seeking reelection with the advantages that come with it. He has raised roughly three times as much as Democratic nominee Kaylee Peterson and holds a wide cash edge, while independent Sarah Zabel has also raised money that may draw from the same pool of voters. July surveys showed Fulcher ahead by margins ranging from five to twenty-one points, and prediction markets give Peterson only about a three percent chance of winning.\n\nPeterson has campaigned on healthcare costs and public lands, and a favorable national environment could trim Fulcher's margin somewhat. But no expert ratings list the race, polling is sparse and dated, and the fundamentals point firmly to the incumbent. The realistic question is the size of Fulcher's victory, not which party wins the seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -16.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0123, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0169, "margin": -17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0127, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0192, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.006, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0083, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0149, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0221, "margin": -17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0086, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0146, "margin": -